<pdd-reason>Give the Ubuntu browser Finder-inspired skins and optional local backgrounds without reading document contents.</pdd-reason>
<pdd-dependency>core_rust.prompt</pdd-dependency>
<pdd-interface>{"type":"module","module":{"functions":[{"name":"effective_theme","signature":"(theme: &str, items: &[Entry]) -> String"},{"name":"stylesheet","signature":"(theme: &str, image: &Path) -> String"}]}}</pdd-interface>
Implement src/appearance.rs. Provide Silver (light), Midnight (dark), Aurora (blue/green) and Automatic. Automatic uses majority file extensions: pictures -> Aurora; code -> Midnight; otherwise Silver including empty folders. Explicit selection overrides Automatic. MUST NOT inspect file contents, infer private topics, or call network/AI services.
Produce valid GTK 3 CSS with Finder-inspired pale sidebar, compact toolbar, blue selection, clear typography, rounded controls, and readable translucent list panel over optional image. Background images are local files, URI-encoded and CSS-escaped (including apostrophes). Empty/missing image falls back to the selected skin. Keep error feedback and selection readable in every skin. No Apple assets are required.
